      "id": "cebel-i-kumr",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>Cebel-i \u1e32umr</em>:\u00a0<em>\u0130bn Sa\u2018\u012bd</em> and <em>Y\u0101\u1e33\u016bt</em> record it as \u201c\u1e32umr\u201d, with the <em>q\u0101f</em> pronounced with <em>\u1e0damma</em> (u) and the <em>m\u012bm</em> in <em>suk\u016bn</em>.\u00a0Some others define it with <em>fat\u1e25</em> of the <em>q\u0101f</em>, as \u201c\u1e32amer\u201d, saying,\u00a0<em data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"567\">\u201cWithout considering the written form, it resembles bewilderment as it appears to the confused eye.\u00a0</em>It is a mountainous region which is always visible with mist/vapor.\u00a0It is written that this is the place of the source of the <em>N\u012bl-i M\u0131\u1e63r</em> (the Nile of Egypt). [translation]</p>",
